I've never tried this package before but I installed it on 10.4 and
was able to get it to run by doing:

    sudo chgrp staff /usr/games/nethack
    sudo chmod g+s /usr/games/nethack

I don't know what group this package normally uses setgid but it looks
like the data files are owned by group 'staff' so this may work
until there's an official fix...

